# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore — keep build context lean for `docker build` / `fly deploy`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this, every COPY pulls in local node_modules + .nuxt + .output
# trees (gigabytes), slowing the build and leaking dev artifacts into the
# image. We deliberately keep ALL workspace package manifests on disk so
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` matches the lockfile — pruning by
# package would break the install.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Node + tool caches
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.cache

# Build outputs (Dockerfile re-builds them inside the image)
**/.nuxt
**/.output
**/dist
**/.turbo

# Generated Prisma client (regenerated inside the image)
apps/dashboard/server/generated
packages/platform/src/database/prisma/generated

# Editor / OS / VCS
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Local-only / never-image-side. `**/.env` catches apps/*/.env too so dev
# DB credentials and session passwords don't bake into the image — Fly
# secrets are the source of truth at runtime.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
.secrets
.tmp-*

# Repo memory / planning / agent context — not runtime artifacts
.memory
.research
.plans
.agent
.templates
.claude

# Documentation
**/*.md
LICENSE
